    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0723" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5967: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-01-28T13:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                                1925—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 28—10:15
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>49. My 47, January 27, 3 p.m. Following extract from radiogram dated 3:20 p.m.,
                    January 27, from Admiral McVay: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Senior naval officers met and agreed following message to <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Carlisle</hi> at Woosung: “Send an officer
                            together with an officer from United States destroyer at Woosung to
                            inform commanding officer, Woosung fort, that senior naval officers
                            cannot accept the wireless warning issued last night, Monday, January
                            26th, closing the forts during the night constituting an interference
                            with foreign shipping. Senior naval officers will, if necessary, escort
                            foreign vessels. Also inform him that search of any vessels including
                            Chinese inside Whangpoo River cannot be tolerated. Limit of the Whangpoo
                            River being [beacon] on outer end submerged breakwater. Inform him that
                            if foreign vessels are interfered with, we are prepared for making
                            immediate reprisal.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d422-f1"/></p></quote></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d422-f1" n="12" xml:id="d422-f1-content">
                <p>The Minister in China in telegram No. 50, Jan. 29, 1 p.m., reported that Admiral
                    McVay telegraphed on January 28: “Woosung fort has agreed to abide by notice
                    sent yesterday.” (File No. 893.00/5972.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
